# missing_number:
# CSES 1083, Missing Number (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1083), in our own words:
# the numbers 1 to n were written down in some order and one of them was lost; given n
# and the remaining n - 1 numbers, which number is missing. The input is the binary
# natural n (corpora/library/binary/natural), at least 1, and a Scott list
# (corpora/library/prelude/list) of the n - 1 other numbers, each a binary natural
# from 1 to n, no two equal; the answer is a binary natural. Part of the CSES port's
# fourth batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the missing number is the k from 1 to n that
# no number of the list equals; the program tries k = 1, 2, … in turn, asking of each
# whether the list holds it, and answers the first that it does not, which is the only
# one, since the list holds n - 1 different numbers of the n. Its reading takes up to
# n times the length of the list comparisons; the replacement the family asks for is
# the sum formula, n (n + 1) / 2 less the sum of the list, in the length of the list
# steps, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since the search
# consumes the gap n - k (it answers 0 past n, which no input of the problem reaches)
# and every other recursion consumes a finite list; the branches that a Scott boolean
# discards are never read. The program calls no subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V
# by the soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of
# Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an answer, P
# ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while Böhm's
# theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and applying
# both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items candidate
    . items false λ head tail. merge_binary_equality head candidate true (self tail candidate)
  )
λ occurs
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ upper numbers
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self candidate
        . binary_less_than upper candidate binary_zero
          (occurs numbers candidate (self (merge_binary_increment candidate)) candidate)
      ) one
  )
λ missing_number
. export missing_number
